  "question": {
    "text": "<p>In the figure, a ladder of mass m is shown leaning against a wall. It is in static equilibrium making an angle <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">θ</mi></math> with the horizontal floor. The coefficient of friction between the wall and the ladder is <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">μ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> and that between the floor and the ladder is <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">μ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> . The normal reaction of the wall on the ladder is <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> and that of the floor is <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> If the ladder is about to slip, then<br ><br/><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/image5-db0e8d55-3424-4441-aa8f-7b932f90418c.png\"/></p>",
    "image": null
